WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.340
The Marketplace and contribution database are complementary tools.

2
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.360
Use the Marketplace to explore products, suppliers and the recognition status recorded

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.300
for a named offering.

4
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.060
Use the contribution database to find specifications and design collateral, including the

5
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.980
revision that governs an interface claim.

6
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.080
Don't flatten those into a single certified or not certified decision.

7
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.640
A product listing doesn't establish that your selected equipment, accessories and site

8
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.540
conditions were all qualified together.

9
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:31.120
A published design contribution doesn't mean every manufactured assembly built around its

10
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.240
name has demonstrated the same performance.

11
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.100
In the evidence record, capture the product identity, status, source document and

12
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.200
revision separately.

13
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.640
Ask the supplier which claims the submitted reports support and where configuration

14
00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.500
differences remain.

15
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.120
If a listing or document has changed since the proposal was prepared,

16
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.400
resolve that difference before acceptance.

17
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.480
These tools make discovery and traceability easier.

18
00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.420
The integrator still needs evidence for the assembled system and the operator

19
00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:00.340
still needs acceptance against the actual deployment conditions.

